# Trivy findings decided against on purpose (Oct 13, 2026). Every entry needs a reason;
# remove an entry when the decision changes. Open on purpose: AZU-0058 (geo-redundant
# storage, a cost decision) and DS-0002 (container as non-root, to be tested on UAT with
# the Azure Files mount first).

# Storage account reachable from all networks: App Service mounts the Azure Files share
# over the public endpoint; closing it needs VNet integration (a larger change).
AZU-0012

# Storage analytics logging: extra cost; the store logs and audits on its own.
AZU-0057

# App Service authentication (Easy Auth): the store has its own sign-in, and the catalog
# and API must stay reachable for Power PDF clients without an Entra ID login.
AZU-0003

# Client certificates: Power PDF clients across many companies use the public catalog.
AZU-0001

# Managed identity: the template sets "identity": {"type": "SystemAssigned"} on the site
# (finding not reproducible).
AZU-0002

# Blob soft delete: set in the child resource storageAccounts/blobServices "default"
# (deleteRetentionPolicy 7 days); Trivy's ARM check does not read that resource.
AZU-0056

# Docker HEALTHCHECK: App Service checks the container itself (healthCheckPath /api/ping
# in infra/azuredeploy.json); the aspnet base image has no curl for a HEALTHCHECK.
DS-0026
